import "core"
import "llm"
import "artifacts/lcm/page.ct"


# What [/Llm/lcm] asks a model, built without asking one: a page as it was written, with its
  annotations shown, what is wrong with it noted where it is wrong, and then the question.
  The page is @artifacts/lcm/page.ct@, written to be wrong in each way a prompt notes: a print
  with no golden, a print whose golden is stale, an annotation that fails, and a definition the
  compiler cannot build. It is a page of its own rather than this one, because a fixture's prints
  are its tests, which the suite runs, and these are written to fail. The page offers the prompt
  about itself as [prompt], since the page a call is written on is the one the compiler hands it.
main{io -> IO}= io.println(msg= prompt(input= "What does double do?")).exit(val= 0)
